---
// Astro's static build now produces real per-route files, so nginx's old
// `try_files $uri /index.html` SPA-fallback trick is no longer needed for deep
// links — but it IS still needed for one thing: the legacy App.jsx's own `*`
// route renders Home instead of a real 404 (a pre-existing quirk, not something
// this migration set out to change). Mounting the legacy app here reproduces
// that exact behavior for any unmatched URL — its router still reads the real
// browser location and falls through to Home — while Astro's build also emits
// this as dist/404.html, so nginx can point its 404 handler at that file to keep
// unmatched paths working the same way they do today. See the astrobuild-migration
// PR description for the one-line nginx config change this needs.
import LegacyShell from '../layouts/LegacyShell.astro';
---

<LegacyShell />
